.TH "RECORD\-IMAGE\-TBOX\.PY" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-image\-tbox\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-image\-tbox\.py\fR \fB>\fR \fIoutput\.owl\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-image\-tbox\.py\fR generates an OWL ontology, in OWL Functional\-Style Syntax, describing the structure (TBOX) of the RECORD/SSREPI database schema itself \(em tables, columns, primary keys, foreign keys, and the relationships between tables \(em rather than the data contained within it\. This is distinct from the other \fBrecord\-image\-*\.py\fR scripts, which visualise the \fIdata\fR graph; this script documents the \fIschema\fR\.
.P
The script writes the generated ontology directly to standard output, in three phases:
.IP "1." 4
A fixed ontology header declaring core classes (\fBColumn\fR, \fBForeignKey\fR, \fBPrimaryKey\fR, \fBTable\fR, \fBKey\fR) and object properties (\fBhasForeignKey\fR, \fBhasPart\fR, \fBhasPrimaryKey\fR, \fBmanyToMany\fR, \fBpartOf\fR, \fBrelation\fR), along with their domains, ranges, and labels\.
.IP "2." 4
For each relationship returned by \fBssrepi\.derive_edges()\fR, declarations of the source and target table classes, their primary or foreign key classes, and an object property linking them \(em classified as either \fBmanyToMany\fR (if the edge has a \fBjoin\fR) or \fBrelation\fR otherwise\.
.IP "3." 4
For each table and column set returned by \fBssrepi\.labels()\fR, declarations of the table class and each of its column classes, asserting that each column is part of its table\.
.IP "" 0
.P
The output is closed with a final \fB)"\fR to complete the \fBOntology(\|\.\|\.\|\.)\fR declaration opened in the header\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero (with a \fBSyntaxError\fR) under Python 3, since the script is written using Python 2 print\-statement syntax (see BUGS)\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
The script inherits all database connection environment variables from the \fBssrepi\fR library\. Refer to \fBssrepi\.py\fR for the full list\. No database connection is opened directly in this script; schema information is obtained via \fBssrepi\.derive_edges()\fR and \fBssrepi\.labels()\fR\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
Writes a complete OWL ontology in Functional\-Style Syntax to standard output\. Redirect to a file to capture it:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-image\-tbox\.py > schema\-tbox\.owl
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Generate the schema TBOX and save it to a file:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-image\-tbox\.py > schema\-tbox\.owl
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Generate the TBOX and validate it with an OWL tool (e\.g\. ROBOT):
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-image\-tbox\.py > schema\-tbox\.owl
robot validate \-\-input schema\-tbox\.owl
.fi
.IP "" 0
