.SH "BUGS"
\fBThis script is written in Python 2 and will not run under Python 3\.\fR Every \fBprint\fR statement uses the bare Python 2 form (\fBprint "\|\.\|\.\|\."\fR) rather than the Python 3 function call form (\fBprint("\|\.\|\.\|\.")\fR)\. This will raise a \fBSyntaxError\fR immediately on any Python 3 interpreter, which is what the shebang (\fB#!/usr/bin/env python3\fR) requests\. The shebang and the script body are therefore mutually inconsistent\.
.P
This script imports \fBssrepi\fR rather than \fBrecord\fR, consistent with the other "image" scripts but inconsistent with \fBrecord\-image\-project\.py\fR\.
.P
The module\-level imports include \fBgraphviz\fR, \fBos\fR, \fBre\fR, \fBrandom\fR, and \fBstring\fR, none of which are used anywhere in the script body\.
.P
The variable \fBsourceForeignKey\fR is computed twice: once unconditionally near the top of the loop body, and again inside the \fBelse\fR branch when \fB"join" not in edgeValue\.keys()\fR\. The first computation is dead code\.
.P
Variable names \fBsourceClass\fR, \fBtargetClass\fR, \fBsourceKey\fR, \fBtargetKey\fR, \fBtargetPrimaryKey\fR, and \fBsourceForeignKey\fR are all assigned the \fIstring\fR result of \fBgetattr(\|\.\|\.\|\.)()\fR or string concatenation, but are named as if they held class objects\. This is a naming inconsistency that makes the logic difficult to follow (the author's own inline comment \(em "you need to tidy this up, because it is virtually impossible to read" \(em confirms this)\.
.P
The indentation inside the multi\-line string literals for \fBsourcePrimaryKey\fR and \fBsourceForeignKey\fR blocks contains inconsistent leading whitespace (some \fBSubClassOf\fR lines are indented with extra spaces relative to their siblings), which does not affect the generated OWL syntax but suggests the string templates were edited carelessly\.
.P
The script assumes \fBssrepi\.derive_edges()\fR and \fBssrepi\.labels()\fR succeed and return well\-formed dictionaries; there is no error handling if the schema cannot be introspected or if \fBsource\fR/\fBtarget\fR strings do not contain the expected \fBClassName(key)\fR format, in which case \fB\.index("(")\fR will raise a \fBValueError\fR\.
.P
No \fBssrepi\.connect_db()\fR / \fBdisconnect_db()\fR calls are present, unlike the other \fBrecord\-image\-*\.py\fR scripts, suggesting \fBderive_edges()\fR and \fBlabels()\fR operate on static schema metadata rather than a live connection \(em this should be confirmed and documented in \fBssrepi\.py\fR\.
